//BUG="FEEDBACK.md 1.3 — an integer literal too large for i32 becomes a float"
//OUT="3000000000"

// string_to_token (src/compiler/tokenizer.rs) tries i32, then the `…L` suffix
// for i64, and then falls through to parse::<f32>(). A plain decimal integer
// that does not fit in i32 therefore becomes a float: the generated C says
// `long double var0; var0 = 3000000000;` and this program prints
// 3000000000.000000000. The literal still looks like an integer in the C
// output, which makes it very hard to spot.
//
// Fix: promote to i64, or reject with "integer literal too large, use `…L`".
// If you choose to reject, this case becomes an //ERR any + //MSG one.

fn main
    x = 3000000000
    out "{x}"
